### 1. Create a User
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "IvanDev",
  "email": "ivan@budgetescapes.edu",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 2. Create a Post (Make sure the user_id matches the ID generated from step 1)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": 1,
  "title": "A Weekend in Berlin",
  "slug": "weekend-in-berlin",
  "content": "Found an amazing currywurst stand near the East Side Gallery.",
  "category": "City"
}

### Login User
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ivan@budgetescapes.edu",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 3. Fetch All Posts (Your [] should now be full of data!)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/posts


### 1. Login to the Application
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ivan@budgetescapes.edu",
  "password": "securepassword123"
}

### 2. Logout of the Application
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/logout